      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I will say, I have gotten very much used to the current style of movement, and as long as it remains an option to change between types, I'm all for this, even if I'd still use the old system.\n\nI even made my VR minecraft controls with Vivecraft use the same controls as VRchat, and found I was able to stay in VR for longer periods of time.\n\nI am a strong support that VR needs to have highly customizable controls, so one can match a control style they can be comfortable in, else motion sickness will kick in, when things are unfamiliar.\n\nmost video games can get away with having varied controls, and onyl creates mild annoyance, but VR it's much more important.  A game can be completely unplayable because of nausea.\n\nVRchat is my most used platform for VR, so I aim to set my controls as close to it as possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
